A||N||19||The Dealer||???||||1||
Z||000000||The Dealer||06-29-2001||12:18 PM||||I was talking to the guy that has my Fiero, I'm buying it off him soon and got some news that makes my stomach roll.<P>He tells me it has developed a knock, that sounds like a ping.  This is very suprising b/c the engine was just rebuilt.  It is a 2.8 V6 with a 4 spd manual. <P>I can think of a few things that it could be, but being that it was freshly rebuilt, those options don't make sense.  Any ideas?<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000001||Devotshka||06-29-2001||12:25 PM||||Were the exhaust manifolds replaced/repaired during the rebuild?  the front one has a tendency to get a crack that some people say sounds like a light knock/ping.... i personally say it sounds like a sweing machine.  Might be worth investigating.  Also check that the timing is not out of adjustment, that can cause a ping in some motors, not sure about in fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||06-29-2001||12:31 PM||||Doesn't sound right...unless he botched the break-in.  I'd have the timing checked.  If the knocking is what I think it is it may mean one of the bearing are shot.  If so you can drive the car about 20 to 50 miles before it'll lock up like mine did.  However, it is hard to say since there is no way for me to hear the car.  More likely one of the lifters didn't fill or the rockers aren't adjusted properly.||||reg||1
Z||000003||The Dealer||06-29-2001||12:49 PM||||I know.... it just doesn't sound right....<P>I talked to him again and he had his step dad listen to it, who apparently knows engines, and says it sounds like a valve.... He's going to throw some treatment in it.. But it still doesn't make much sense.<P>The Dealer||||reg||8
Z||000004||TRiAD||06-29-2001||12:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Dealer:<BR><B>...he had his step dad listen to it, who apparently knows engines...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Be VERY careful in this. I would be looking for a different car. If this guy's one of those shadetree <I>"I think I know what I'm doing, it's just like a Briggs 'n Stratton, right?"</I> guys, you won't want to be within 100 yards of this car. <P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||The Dealer||06-29-2001||12:57 PM||||i undrestand what you are saying.. I'm being very cautious.... I told him I want to listen to it before I decide....<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000006||JamesWM83||06-29-2001||02:01 PM||||I'm the guy he's gettin the Fiero off of. If there's anything you can tell me to check or to look into replacing let me know. I want this car to be running like it did when I bought it. I didn't rebuild it... the guy that owned it before I bought it, completely rebuilt the engine. I'm gonna check the front manifold for a crack like was said, and I'll check out the lifters as well. My step dad did say it sounded like a valve was knocking. It doesn't sound right to me. But I'm looking into anyways. Sparks do come from the manifold by the way... crack you think? Let me know on things to check. I don't want him feeling screwed. I'm giving him the car, with the promise that I can buy his off him. That's the deal I offered him after this began happening. Some of the plugs I just pulled out weren't even tight, I took 4 out by hand. I'm gonna do some deeper research now, let me know if you guys think of anything. THanks. LAyter||||reg||1
Z||000007||TRiAD||06-29-2001||02:22 PM||||James. I appreciate your not taking offense to what I said, it's nice when people know you don't mean any. <P>I think it's admirable that you sound very concerned about the condition of the car when you sell it. <P>How long have you had it? I would be thinking of how to handle the previous owner, who rebuilt it, if you bought it recently. It does NOT sound good...I would be looking into making him refund you, and go find a better car. He obviously had no idea what he was doing, and should never have rebuilt a motor. <P>I hope this all works out well for both of you. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||JamesWM83||06-30-2001||12:21 AM||||Thanks... no offense taken. I do care about him and what happens with this car. I've loved it since the day I bought it. I've had it for about 1 and a half months. I investigated it today, and found some things wrong.<BR>1) 4 of the 6 spark plugs I was able to take out by hand the whole way. <BR>2) #2 cylinder plug was covered in oil<BR>3)front exhaust manifold collector was not even bolted the the block on the fat left. <P>Could these things be why it's doing that noise? I'm gonna fix it all tomorrow and see what happens. Thanks for everything I've gotten so far. Lates<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||maryjane||06-30-2001||09:32 PM||||Ditto everything Triad said. I've bought cars before and found stuff wrong I KNOW the owner knew about and "forgot" to mention. I don't mind buyin something that needs work, it's just I'd like toknow about it. I never sell anything without being completly open,even if it means losing the sale. It's nice to see someone to do right. Good luck with your troubleshooting.||||reg||14
Z||000010||voyagerspe||07-01-2001||12:28 AM||||I ran into a knock that you would swear  was a rod knock.  It turned out to be a loose flywheel (at the crank). I dropped the cradle, pulled the motor and tightend the bolts(i applied locktight) and reinstalled.  Engine runs great, no knocks.  If your finding loose stuff on the engine I would investigate the flywheel.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||JayUSA77||07-01-2001||12:33 AM||||Hey dealer, look at the knock as a oppurtunity to knock the price of the car down major unless they fix it.  if he want 2500 for example offer him 2000.  I mean now that is has a knock its going to be hard to sell ne ways so you would be doing him a favor.<BR>-J<BR>86' Fiero GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||The Dealer||07-01-2001||03:14 AM||||understood, ty... I have my grounds covered on the price drop....<P><BR>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000013||Greg Piet||07-01-2001||03:21 AM||||<B>BACK THE TRUCK UP</B><P>Are you seriously telling this forum that you are gonna buy a car from some schmo who <B>SAYS</B> it is a fresh motor that has a knock, and the solution is to put in <B>magical mystery valve fixin' goo</B>????????  <P>You had better bookmark the tech section of pennocks on every computer you might ever use, and start working on making more descriptive topics.||||reg||1
Z||000014||TRiAD||07-01-2001||09:39 AM||||Greg, the seller of the car on the forum is NOT who did the rebuild. HE'S the one that got schmo'ed. He was in the process of selling it to someone else here, and discovered the previous work was not done correctly. <BR>As long as they're both honest and they're both informed, we don't have grounds to advise against the sale. <BR>We can suggest the seller return it to the guy who sold it to him (the guy who did the crappy work), and I have.<P>Now we just watch and hope for the best. You were on the right track, just the wrong sale. It's good to know there are people here who look out for these things though...||||reg||1
Z||000015||Indiana_resto_guy||07-01-2001||10:46 AM||||On a more serious note to the seller or the buyer.<BR>Try a 'new' set of plug wires and plugs. If the car has few miles on the rebuild look into readjusting the lifters as they have a tendency to loosen up a bit within the first few hundred miles or so.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Mach10||07-01-2001||03:07 PM||||What worries me is the "plug covered in oil" That can't be good. Then again, you can get a head redone for a couple of hundred anyway, so if the rest of the car's good, it might be worth the shot?||||reg||7
Z||000017||JamesWM83||07-01-2001||05:24 PM||||As far as the price drop goes... I've told the dealer that I would give him the car for free, and even pay for him to get it home... as long as hge promised to sell me his car in return.<P>I will look at the flywheel today. AND... I just put new plugs and wires in it... so... meh. I will check the lifters, and I will check the rocker arms.... as soon as I get the time... probly today. Man.. this is gonna suck.. but it's fun I guess... hehe. <P>If he doesn't take the car, it's gettin a 350 and it's goin show...  but I really want his car.... it's my dream car, the same as he has always wanted a Fiero. He can't find one cheaper... FREE! <P>Anyways... I'll check all that stuff.... and I'll get a new oil change... and we'll see what happens. Any thoughts on that noise maybe coming from the manifold with no bolts in it? Let me know anything you can think of. Thanks. Lates<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||87GTZ34||07-01-2001||10:23 PM||||How many miles on this 'fresh' rebuild???  All of those problems sound like the person that did the rebuild was somewhat shady...  Plugs in hand tight???  I bought a second car ('87 GT) in Feb from the 'original owner' who had the motor rebuilt 65K miles ago.  I've already redone the top end as one valve was burned and on 3 others the seats were pitted.  If I did work on a motor that didn't last 65K mi I be embarrassed as...  I Just put a timing chain on it and seal & sleeve too (this didn't wear out in 65K btw).  The harmonic balancer wasn't much more than hand tight so this is more evidence that the 'original owner' brought the car to the meat dept. (butcher shop) for repairs and I am just wondering what other 'surprises' are in store...  Moral of the story: dealer, hold off on this car; James, you need to go back to the seller to see if he wants to give you some money back to cover repairs or go to court.  GL||||reg||1
Z||000019||JamesWM83||07-02-2001||09:02 AM||||The guy I got it off of dropped 600 off the price because I've had these problems lately. My dad's friend.. who is a liscensed mechaninc said it's lifters. It's not even a knocking, it's a rattling. It's not a rod, we know that. And it's nothin else MAJOR. The car runs and drives fin. It occasionally dies... that's all. Usually starts right up, and runs strong. Even with this problem it's runnin 15's. I just hope the dealer takes this car... I love it, but I need a car that more than 2 people can get in. Especially now.... I'll go into detail if I need to on that right there. But I need to have a back seat. And I've always wanted a Z26 anyways, and he still gets the car for free. He said he wanted to use it as a project anyways... heh. I haven't been able to get ahold of him lately. I'll try later today. LAtes.<P>||||reg||1
